---
import SiteShell from "../layouts/SiteShell.astro";
---

<SiteShell title="Submit a recipe">
  <section class="page-heading">
    <h1>Submit a recipe</h1>
    <p>Contribute pinned Lathe inputs that can regenerate a CLI with its embedded Skill, catalog, and reviewable proof.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="submit-layout">
    <article class="doc-page">
      <div class="process-grid">
        <div>
          <span class="panel-label">01</span>
          <h2>Shape the recipe</h2>
          <p>Keep source inputs small, pinned, and reviewable.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <span class="panel-label">02</span>
          <h2>Generate proof</h2>
          <p>Catalog, Skill, build metadata, and smoke checks must derive from the recipe.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <span class="panel-label">03</span>
          <h2>Open the PR</h2>
          <p>Submit the recipe as source of truth, with generated outputs treated as evidence.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <h2>Required shape</h2>
      <pre><code>recipes/&lt;name&gt;/
  lathe.yaml
  cli.yaml
  specs/sources.yaml
  overlays/
  README.md</code></pre>

      <h2>Rules</h2>
      <ul class="checklist">
        <li>Submit reproducible recipes, not generated code as source.</li>
        <li>Pin upstream specs in <code>specs/sources.yaml</code>.</li>
        <li>Describe auth requirements in <code>lathe.yaml</code> and <code>README.md</code>.</li>
        <li>Keep overlays focused on command names, grouping, summaries, aliases, and parameter help.</li>
        <li>Add a smoke intent that proves catalog search works.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Generated evidence</h2>
      <p>Registry automation publishes macOS, Linux, and Windows CLI binaries with embedded Skills, catalog snapshots, build metadata, and static website data. Those outputs must remain reproducible from the recipe.</p>

      <h2>Reference recipe</h2>
      <p>Use <code>recipes/daocloud-dce</code> as the first real template for a multi-source API with auth and overlays.</p>
    </article>

    <aside class="submit-aside">
      <span class="panel-label">Review gate</span>
      <p>The registry accepts recipe inputs first. Generated outputs are useful only when they can be reproduced from the pinned recipe.</p>
      <div class="command-strip" aria-label="Submit command preview">
        <span>$</span>
        <code>npm run generate && npm run build</code>
      </div>
      <a class="button primary block" href="https://github.com/lathe-cli/lathe-registry">Open repository</a>
    </aside>
  </section>
</SiteShell>
